"Connect your real Amazon account"
"You are using the upload route, so none of this is needed. This guide is only for connecting Amazon directly, which is not switched on."
"Amazon controls who may upload invoices. These steps follow Amazon's developer documentation; confirm each screen name in Seller Central, since Amazon renames menus."
"1. Use a professional seller account you own"
"Registered with your own tax ID. Never use an employer's or a client's account without their written consent."
"2. In VAT Calculation Service (VCS), choose \"I will upload my own invoices\""
"Amazon only accepts uploaded invoices from sellers on this option. Otherwise uploads fail with FeatureNotAvailable (error 79509, \"closed beta\")."
"3. Register as an SP-API developer and request the Tax Invoicing role"
"This is a restricted role that Amazon reviews. Approval can take time, so request it early. Without it, reading orders works but uploading does not."
"4. Create a private app and authorise it for your own seller account"
"Copy the LWA client ID, client secret and refresh token. Paste them in the Connect screen. They are stored encrypted. Never send them in chat or email."
"5. Press Sync now"
"InvoiceGuard reads Amazon's VAT invoice report, checks each buyer VAT number in the EU VIES service, issues the invoice and uploads it. Invalid VAT numbers are held, not uploaded."
"6. Supported stores for uploads"
"Spain, UK, France, Netherlands, Germany, Italy, Switzerland, Poland (per Amazon's VCS error documentation)."
"InvoiceGuard does not give tax advice. Ask your gestor about invoice content and VAT treatment."
